# A RESCUE PAST THE 71 HOURS (docs/STORY.md; slice 1 step 6). The same yard and
# the same three housings as tours/rescue.tour, but whoever the plan is holding
# has been held eighty hours: past Taken.RUN_HOURS the plan has run them long
# enough to replace them, and what walks out of the dark yard is not who was
# carried in. The glass says so, flat, at the moment they walk out.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/rescue-late.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --held=axe_felling --carried=1:80
#
# `--carried=1:80` stages one person held eighty hours at the first depot with a
# village in its region (45_taken). Shot the moment they are freed, because the
# glass keeps two lines and the chapter's and the key's come straight after.

coast calm
at rescue:yard
wait 1.0
await held_here 6
press use 5.5
await works_part 14
at rescue:yard_breaker
wait 0.5
press use 5.5
await works_open:2 14
at rescue:yard_coolant
wait 0.5
press use 5.5
await works_broken 14
await freed 6
shot 01-the-yard-goes-dark-and-they-walk-out-empty with works,works_dark
